# Checkouts materialize LF on every platform. Every generator and gate in this
# repository emits and compares LF, and a source pin that spans a line break
# cannot match a CRLF working tree. The eol attribute overrides core.autocrlf,
# so a clean clone behaves the same with or without that global setting.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Byte-identical vendored copy of the uws protocol schema: the parity test
# hashes the working-tree file against the hash recorded from the uws commit,
# so line-ending normalization on checkout would fail the gate on every fresh
# clone.
protocol.schema.json -text

# The conformance vector and the golden trace corpus are byte-compared by
# their tests; a CRLF smudge on a fresh autocrlf clone would fail both gates
# on bytes git invented.
test-vectors/*.json -text
test/dst-goldens/*.json -text

# A PKCS#12 bundle is binary by nature; declaring it keeps check-source-bytes
# from reading its DER bytes as control characters in a text file.
*.pfx binary
